---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services — Omnipeak"
  description="Custom web applications, booking and membership systems, rescue of stalled software projects, process automation, and internal tools — fixed-scope projects built by the same person you explain your business to."
>
  <section class="section page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>What Omnipeak builds</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Whatever your business needs, not what's on a menu. Every project runs the same way:
        you explain how your business works to the person who will build it, and you get a
        fixed scope, a fixed price, and a system you own.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="card card--raised specialty">
        <p class="specialty__label"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--accent-teal);" aria-hidden="true"></span>Deepest specialty</p>
        <h2>Booking, membership &amp; billing systems</h2>
        <p class="muted">
          The hardest kind of small-business software. Systems for businesses that run on
          reservations, recurring memberships, and recurring payments, built around how your
          business actually prices and schedules, not how an off-the-shelf app assumes you do.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>Reservations and slot logic, including time-based and peak pricing</li>
          <li>Memberships with recurring billing, pauses, and cancellations</li>
          <li>Payments through Stripe, in your own Stripe account</li>
          <li>Multi-location support when you're ready to grow</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="specialty__proof">
          Running today at <a href="/work/">Smash Factor Lounge</a>, after two previous
          developers couldn't finish it.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        title="And everything else your business runs on"
        subtitle="If it can be explained clearly, it can be scoped and built."
      />
      <div class="rows">
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Custom web applications</h3>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>
              Most businesses have at least one thing they do differently from everyone else. A
              quoting tool, an inventory system, a customer portal, something no one has named
              yet: that's a normal project, not an exception.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Rescuing stalled projects</h3>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>
              For owners who paid for software and got a half-finished system, or a finished one
              nobody can maintain. Omnipeak reads the existing code, gives you an honest written
              assessment of what's salvageable, and then either finishes it or rebuilds it. You
              get a clear answer before any building starts.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Process automation</h3>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>
              The work your staff does by hand every week (copying records between systems,
              chasing failed payments, sending the same reminder emails, rebuilding the same
              spreadsheet) replaced with software that does it on schedule, every time.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Internal tools &amp; admin dashboards</h3>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>
              The numbers you check every morning and the records your staff updates all day, in
              one place instead of scattered across spreadsheets, inboxes, and someone's memory.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row">
          <h3>Ongoing maintenance</h3>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>
              After launch, Omnipeak can keep improving your system and handling bugs as they
              come in, tracked and dealt with right away. Or you can hand it to anyone you
              choose: the documentation and ownership terms make both options real.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dim">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        title="Fixed scope, fixed price, in writing"
        subtitle="Every project starts with a written proposal. You know what you're getting and what it costs before any work begins."
      />
      <div class="pillars">
        <div class="pillar">
          <h3>What will be built</h3>
          <p>A plain-English description of the system and what it will do for your business.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <h3>What it will cost</h3>
          <p>One fixed price. Not hourly billing that drifts, not an open-ended retainer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar">
          <h3>When it will be done</h3>
          <p>A delivery date, with working software to look at along the way.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
